         measured: pointwise: gamma_v(20 kAU) = 1.0408; registered bracket: 1.095-1.111; the difference ~0.06-0.07 is the additive-law vs two-body-solve SYSTEMATIC, named in L240's own limits and quantified here
         reading : recorded honestly: the pointwise form UNDERSTATES the bracket because it treats the pair's field as a local scalar rather than solving the two-body deep-MOND problem. The BINNED PROFILE (Part B) uses the same pointwise form throughout, so its SHAPE and RISE are internally consistent and comparable to the observed profile up to the same systematic factor; the registered bracket remains the reference prediction, and the profile's rise-from-1.00-to-~1.05 structure is the pointwise form's own, consistent with the bracket's scaling direction

